  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer over-read in mod_ssl OCSP requests\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-44185.patch: in send_request() in\n       modules/ssl/ssl_util_ocsp.c, advance the write pointer by the number\n       of bytes actually sent instead of the total remaining length so a\n       short write to an attacker controlled OCSP responder can no longer\n       read past the end of the stack buffer. Backported from httpd commit\n       32b7e2e66477020ba75b78ab43fb8890ec292ad2 (SVN r1934919).\n     - CVE-2026-44185\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in mod_heartmonitor\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-46729.patch: in hm_handler() in\n       modules/cluster/mod_heartmonitor.c, reject requests when the module\n       is not active or the body exceeds MAX_MSG_LEN, require the busy and\n       ready parameters, and parse port, busy and ready with strtol() so a\n       crafted unicast heartbeat can no longer dereference a NULL pointer.\n       Backported from httpd commit 7b12a7936ec439b3e1f5fc36cfacf5b915eb652c\n       (SVN r1938654).\n     - CVE-2026-46729",
